<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct M2+CD money supply up 3.7 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct M2+CD money supply up 3.7 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.7 percent in October from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>				OCT PRELIM  SEPT REVISED AUG</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2 + CDs    +3.7	  +3.5	  + 3.7</p>
<p>    M1		     +11.5	 +12.2	  +13.8</p>
<p>    CDs		     +58.9	 +25.5	  +40.3</p>
<p>				OCT PRELIM  AUG REVISED AUG</p>
<p> Broadest money measure +3.7	  +3.6	  + 3.8</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>				OCT PRELIM  AUG REVISED AUG</p>
<p> Adjusted M2 + CDs	+4.0	  +0.9	  +2.5</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>				OCT PRELIM  SEPT REVISED AUG</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2+CDs     555.2 trln  556.1 trln 556.9 trln</p>
<p>    M1		     162.5 trln  163.6 trln 163.4 trln</p>
<p>    CDs		     16.0 trln   13.6 trln  13.1 trln</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity  1,124.1 trln1,121.9 trln1,121.4 trln</p>
